## Release Preview

This automated PR was generated by [Callisto](https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto). Merging this PR will publish the updated packages to their release targets.

### 📊 Release Summary

| Package | Ecosystem | Current | Target | Bump | Reason |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `pkg-a` | `unknown` | `1.0.0` | **`1.0.1`** | 🟢 `patch` | Changeset (`brave-eagles-race`, `radiant-pandas-roar`) |
| `pkg-b` | `unknown` | `1.0.0` | **`1.0.1`** | 🟢 `patch` | 4 changesets |

> [!NOTE]
> **2 package(s)** queued for versioning. All changes are backward compatible.

### 📦 What's Changing

**3 change(s) across 2 package(s):**

#### 🟢 Patch

<details>
<summary>Patch: 3 changes</summary>

- **Python ranges keep their precision when a bound has a suffix.** A dependent requirement whose bound carries a post, dev or pre-release suffix is now rewritten at the precision it was written with, in any epoch.

  - `>=1.2.3.post1,<1.3` becomes `>=1.2.4,<1.3` instead of widening to `<2`.
  - `~=1.2.post1` becomes `~=1.2` instead of narrowing to `~=1.2.1`.

  Affects `pkg-a`

- **`pre enter` and `pre exit` stage only their own `pre.json`.** A changesets directory whose name contains glob characters, such as `notes*`, no longer stages a neighbouring tracked `notes-other/pre.json` as well.

  Affects `pkg-a`

- `pkg-b`: Associated changesets: `a`, `b`, `c`, `d`

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>Release Workflow Instructions</b></summary>

- **Merging this PR**: Merging into `main` will automatically publish all updated packages to their release registries.
- **Adding more changesets**: If additional changesets are pushed to `main`, Callisto will automatically re-calculate and update this PR.
- **Manual edits**: You can make manual adjustments directly on the `callisto/version-packages` branch if needed.

</details>
